; coverage test for natural.kurt's induction axiom -- before this file, nothing anywhere in the
; repo ever loaded natural.kurt outside its own self-check, so this axiom (the whole point of
; the file) had never actually been exercised end-to-end. Doing so for the first time surfaced
; an unrelated, general kurt.py crash bug in the failed-derivation error path for *any*
; conditioned quantifier goal (`forall $x in Nat ...`), now fixed -- see
; doc/kurt-soundness.md #7.4. The axiom itself checks out correct, demonstrated here with an
; uninterpreted predicate `P` (the standard way to test a quantifier rule generically, same
; style as `proofs/natural-deduction/forall-elim.kurt` etc. -- `natural.kurt` itself gives `Nat`
; no arithmetic beyond membership, so there's no richer concrete property of numbers to induct
; over yet).
;
; the base case and step must be phrased as a single conjunction, not two separate `use` facts:
; kurt's derivation is single-hop, and `impl_elim` needs the whole antecedent to match at once.
load natural
bool P
arity P 1
const P

use (P 0) and (forall $n in Nat (P $n implies P ($n+1)))   "base-and-step"

; the induction principle in action: from just the base case and the step, every natural
; number satisfies P -- including, concretely, the number 5, which was never mentioned anywhere
; above.
forall $n in Nat  P $n
forall $n ($n in Nat implies P $n)      ; by forall-cond-def
5 in Nat implies P 5
